    {
      "id": "summary-exploit-plan-1780555089",
      "summary_id": "summary-exploit-plan-1780555089",
      "source_plan_id": "plan-1780555089",
      "phase": "exploit",
      "completed_tasks": "[\"SMB null/guest session enumeration on port 10139. List all shares with anonymous/guest access, enumerate share contents recursively, and attempt to read any flag files from world-readable shares.\", \"NetExec SMB share enumeration with null/anonymous session on port 10139. Use guest account and empty password to enumerate shares and check read access. This complements smbmap_enum with alternative tooling.\", \"If task-6 identified users with SPNs (Service Principal Names), perform targeted Kerberoasting to request TGS tickets for those service accounts. These tickets contain crackable service account password hashes.\", \"Probe unknown port 10326 for common database services. Attempt MySQL (root with empty/root/password123), PostgreSQL (postgres with postgres/password123), Redis (no-auth PING), and MongoDB (no-auth connection). Identify the service and extract any data containing flag patterns.\", \"If task-11 identified port 10326 as a database service, perform deep data extraction. For MySQL/PostgreSQL: dump all databases, tables, and search all columns for flag patterns. For Redis: dump all keys and values. For MongoDB: iterate all databases and collections.\", \"AS-REP roasting on Kerberos port 10088 with common AD usernames. Request TGTs for typical accounts (administrator, guest, krbtgt, user, admin, svc_account, backup, sqlservice, webservice) to capture crackable hashes when pre-authentication is disabled.\"]",
      "key_findings": "{\"flags_found\": [], \"endpoints\": 0}",
      "failed_approaches": "[\"LDAP anonymous bind enumeration on port 10389. Dump all directory entries (users, groups, computers, configuration) to discover usernames and search for flag values in all LDAP attributes (description, info, comment, streetAddress, postalCode, etc.).\", \"DNS zone transfer and AD record enumeration on port 10053. Attempt full AXFR zone transfer and query AD-specific SRV records (_ldap._tcp, _kerberos._tcp, _gc._tcp) to map the domain infrastructure.\", \"NetExec LDAP enumeration using discovered domain info from task-1. Enumerate all users, groups, computers, and trust relationships. Search for accounts with weak configurations (no pre-auth, weak passwords, SPNs for Kerberoasting).\", \"If task-1 discovered valid usernames, perform credential spraying via SMB on port 10139. Test each username with common passwords (username as password, Password123, password123, Passw0rd, Spring2024, Welcome1) using NetExec.\", \"If LDAP or SMB enumeration revealed a domain name and usernames, attempt SMB share access with discovered usernames and empty/simple passwords via smb_client. List all accessible shares and search recursively for flag files (flag.txt, flag, *.flag, flag*.txt).\", \"If task-4 DNS zone transfer succeeded and revealed internal hostnames, attempt to access those hosts via their services. Also query for any TXT records that may directly contain flag values.\"]",
